{"crc":"c115caac","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in the `_escape_args_and_kwargs` method in `sphinx/ext/napoleon/docstring.py`. When an attribute name ends with an underscore (like `hello_`), it's being escaped as `hello\\_`, which shows a visible backslash in the HTML output.\n\nThe fix should only escape trailing underscores for parameter names (where `*args` and `**kwargs` patterns need escaping), not for attribute names. Let me look at how this method is called.\n\nThe `_escape_args_and_kwargs` method is called from `_consume_field`, which is used for parsing fields in various sections including attributes. The escaping of trailing underscores is meant for parameter names like `*args` and `**kwargs`, but it's incorrectly being applied to attribute names as well.\n\nThe fix should remove the trailing underscore escaping from `_escape_args_and_kwargs` since it's not needed - the underscore at the end of a name doesn't need to be escaped in RST. The escaping of `*` and `**` prefixes is still needed for kwargs.\n\n# path: sphinx/ext/napoleon/docstring.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def _escape_args_and_kwargs(self, name: str) -> str:\n        if name.endswith('_'):\n            name = name[:-1] + r'\\_'\n\n        if name[:2] == '**':\n            return r'\\*\\*' + name[2:]\n        elif name[:1] == '*':\n            return r'\\*' + name[1:]\n        else:\n            return name\n=======\n    def _escape_args_and_kwargs(self, name: str) -> str:\n        if name[:2] == '**':\n            return r'\\*\\*' + name[2:]\n        elif name[:1] == '*':\n            return r'\\*' + name[1:]\n        else:\n            return name\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQVDJ187N2DYD93ZY8RGZMR","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQVDJ12G18F7TMTMRV7PVN8"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786433167.060437}
